    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0794" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg724"/>

                <head>No. 458.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1883-10-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 30, 1883</date>. (Received
                        November 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy,
                    together with a translation, of a circular note, dated the 23d instant,
                    addressed to me by Señor Don <pb facs="0795" n="725" xml:id="pg725"/> J. A. de
                    Lavalle, appointed minister of foreign relations, in which he gives a history of
                    the circumstances attending the establishment of the Iglesias government, and
                    invites recognition. To this note I replied as per copy inclosed herewith.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>S. L. PHELPS.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d457-a1.xml" xpointer="d457-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d457-a2.xml" xpointer="d457-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
